{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Health Care Financing to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents relative to the health care financing matters.","BillNumber":"S2768","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J24","Name":"Joint Committee on Health Care Financing","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24","ResponseDate":"2024-05-03T12:44:14.183"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2768/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, May 6, 2024 -- The committee on Health Care Financing, to whom was referred the Senate Bills promoting consumer choice in health care (Senate, No. 603); relative to community behavioral health centers (Senate, No. 613); and ensuring prompt access to health care (Senate, No. 654) , reports the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2768).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Health Care Financing be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 603, 613, and 654 relative to health care financing matters.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J24","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}